X-WR-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Akhil Reed Amar on Birth Equality and the US Constitution
DTSTART:20260812T180000
DTEND:20260812T193000
DTSTAMP:20260811T183650Z
UID:f00c7af979217ade4001563792cf57@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Akhil Reed Amar on Birth Equality and the US Constitution<br/>
 Wednesday\, August 12th<br/>6:00 pm - 7:30 pm<br/><br/>Renowned constituti
 onal scholar and bestselling author Akhil Reed Amar will offer a wide-angl
 ed and in-depth approach to understanding America’s ever-evolving journe
 y to live up to its central founding moral principle that all people are c
 reated equal. On August 12\, 2026\, from 6:00 to 7:30pm\, the Yale Sterlin
 g Professor of Law and Political Science — whose scholarship is often ci
 ted by Supreme Court Justices across the ideological spectrum — will exp
 lore the enduring relevance of the Constitution. As Americans grapple with
  fundamental questions about democracy and equality\, this timely conversa
 tion continues Hildene’s commitment to fostering thoughtful public dialo
 gue and civic engagement. The first 50 registrants will receive a copy of 
 the second book in Amar’s trilogy\, the recently published and highly pr
 aised Born Equal: Remaking America’s Constitution\, 1840–1920. <br/><b
 r/>6:00 pm - 6:45 pm: Talk<br/>6:45 pm - 7:00 pm: Q&amp\;A<br/>7:05 pm –
  7:30 pm: Book Personalizing<br/><br/>REGISTER ONLINE\n\nSources: Vermont 
 Public
LOCATION:Talks & Readings
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/akhil-reed
 -amar-on-birth-equality-and-the-us-constitution-17-07-2026-11-29-44
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Amplified featuring Troy Millette and the Fire Below with Coll
 in Hagood
DTSTART:20260812T170000
DTEND:20260812T200000
DTSTAMP:20260811T183650Z
UID:d2c914327ddb0fefd152166fcf14a6@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:5 PM: A relative newcomer to the Vermont nightlife scene\, Bur
 lington-based vinyl DJ Collin Hagood is inspired by the days of early MTV 
 and 1980s sounds on the LA radio station KROQ\, curating classic alternati
 ve music spanning genres of new wave\, punk\, post-punk\, goth\, and indus
 trial selections. Whether striking a moody tone or one of joyful vibrance\
 , Hagood aims to create an amusing party vibe for your ears and feet alike
 . <br/><br/>6:30 PM: <br/>Vermont’s TROY MILLETTE &amp\; THE FIRE BELOW 
 are equal parts thoughtful and lively– a cocktail of rock\, pop\, folk\,
  and americana music that grapples with love\, loss\, and the human experi
 ence. <br/><br/>Millette’s emotive and relatable lyrics\, as well as his
  energetic\, banter-filled live performances have made him a staple of div
 es\, clubs\, theaters\, and festivals across the northeast United States a
 nd Quebec. His work as a frontman and solo performer garnered the title of
  Vermont’s “Best Folk Group” from Seven Days Magazine in 2022 and 20
 23 (some guy named Noah Kahan beat them in 2024. No big deal). <br/><br/>H
 is “Errors Tour” and “Less Than 1% of the World Tour” have taken M
 illette to more than 20 states since fall 2023. <br/><br/>Pop into BCA dur
 ing your passeggiata stroll! Mingle with friends and neighbors and enjoy t
 he gallery in a whole new way—alive with vibrant lights\, DJs\, live mus
 ic\, fun drinks\, and immaculate vibes. <br/><br/>Summer in the City is ma
 de possible in part thanks to Underwriters at the Pomerleau Family Foundat
 ion\; Supporters Burlington Telecom\, Myti\, Soundtoys\, and Lake Champlai
 n Chocolates\, and Community Partner American Flatbread Burlington &amp\; 
 Mothership Brewery. Media Sponsors: Seven Days and WCAX.⁠\n\nSources: Ve
 rmont Public
LOCATION:Music: Rock\, Folk\, Jazz and More
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/art-amplif
 ied-featuring-troy-millette-and-the-fire-below-with-collin-hagood-19-06-20
 26-20-16-26
END:VEVENT
