BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DINO FEST at ECHO
DTSTART:20260812T100000
DTEND:20260812T150000
DTSTAMP:20260811T183650Z
UID:1f9784629b30273c71b9cc531a73f7@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Roar into a day packed with all things dinosaurs! Discover how
  these incredible creatures may have lived\, from their daily habits to th
 e asteroid impact that changed life on Earth forever. Meet the survivors: 
 come face-to-face with local species whose ancestors lived alongside the d
 inosaurs — and made it through the extinction event that their dino rela
 tives didn’t. From snapping turtles to sturgeon\, you’ll be surprised 
 who’s still around today.<br/><br/>Don’t forget to explore our Dinosau
 r Safari exhibit before ending your day with some awesome gift shop dino m
 erch!\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Kids & Family
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/dino-fest-
 at-echo-29-07-2026-16-24-44
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fletcher Free Library Book Discussion Group: The Wilderness
DTSTART:20260812T183000
DTEND:20260812T203000
DTSTAMP:20260811T183650Z
UID:045f62ce41955ac047e2740a12fd41@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join other readers at this virtual discussion of The Wildernes
 s by Angela Flournoy.<br/><br/>Contact: Barbara Shatara at bshatara@burlin
 gtonvt.gov to register and to obtain Zoom info.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Location: Chittenden County
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/fletcher-f
 ree-library-book-discussion-group-the-wilderness-05-08-2026-09-49-34
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NXT Rockumentary Film Series
DTSTART:20260812T190000
DTEND:20260812T210000
DTSTAMP:20260811T183650Z
UID:5b106ef7d5be2f712951a60b8b57ae@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the next installment of the NXT Rockumentary Film 
 Series. <br/><br/>This acclaimed music documentary offers a rare\, behind-
 the-scenes look at the creative process and camaraderie that drive a legen
 dary touring act. Captured with a raw\, intimate visual style and immersiv
 e sound\, the film blends performance footage\, candid moments\, and life 
 on the road into a compelling portrait of musicians at work. Its lo-fi aes
 thetic and unfiltered access create an experience that feels both spontane
 ous and deeply authentic\, making it a standout entry in the rock document
 ary genre.<br/><br/>Due to licensing restrictions\, we’re unable to publ
 icly list the film title. To find out what’s screening\, join our mailin
 g list or contact us directly.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Film
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/nxt-rockum
 entary-film-series-10-07-2026-17-30-42
END:VEVENT
